<title>UK: Cadbury Q1 U.S. soft drinks sales up 1 pct.</title>
<headline>Cadbury Q1 U.S. soft drinks sales up 1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British food and drinks group Cadbury Schweppes Plc said on Wednesday that volume sales of soft drinks in the U.S. rose one percent in the first quarter.</p>
<p>Cadburys said volume sales of its Dr Pepper brand rose five percent, while sales of its 7 Up and other brands dropped by two percent.</p>
<p>A Cadbury spokeswoman said soft drinks sales in the Americas account for around 60 percent of the group's beverage sales worldwide. The Americas account for just under 30 percent of total group beverage and confectionery sales.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
